      <h1>
        GO IZUMITA /
        <br />
        泉田剛
      </h1>

      <h2>
        Artist / Architectural Designer
      </h2>

      <p>
        Born in Hirosaki, Aomori, Japan. Based in Tokyo and Hirosaki. His artistic practice involves dismantling and reconstructing disused buildings and structures, transforming them into sculptures and installations. By extracting materials from existing structures and rearranging them into new forms, he explores the relationships between materiality, memory, and space.
      </p>

      <p>
        Drawing on his experience in architectural visualization and graphic design, he also works across exhibition and spatial design, as well as editorial design.
      </p>

      <img
        src="/images/portrait.png"
        alt="Portrait of Go Izumita"
        class="portrait"
      />

      <h1>
        Fields of Practice
      </h1>

      <p>
        With artistic practice at the core of his work, Izumita engages in projects involving architecture, space, and visual expression. His approach spans research, conceptual development, design, and production, adapting to the specific nature of each project.
      </p>

      <h2>
        v Art & Installation
      </h2>

      <p>
        Conception and production of sculptures, installations, and art projects involving existing architecture and materials.
      </p>

      <h2>
        v Spatial & Exhibition Design
      </h2>

